dsh-plugin-bash-wsl

This product includes portions of the bounded terminal session state machine
adapted from `@deepseek-ai/dsh-terminal-bash@0.1.0-rc.6`, Copyright (c) 2026
DeepSeek, under the MIT License. The adapted portions are identified in
`src/terminal/session.ts`; the WSL transport and plugin integration are separate
code in this repository.

The MIT license and copyright notices for the adapted portions are retained in
`LICENSE`.

For the two supported 0.2 hosts, native Git Bash uses the installed official
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-terminal-bash` public backend and startup/session factory.
Its session reuses the bounded state machine in src/terminal/session.ts, with
terminal-protocol reply/drain handling adapted from that component's MIT-licensed
0.2.0-rc.2 / 0.2.1-alpha.1 implementation, Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek. The
actual host's separately installed `@xterm/headless` emulator supplies protocol
replies; it is not bundled here. Additional modes
compose the installed `@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app` Standard preset through the
official preset registry. These upstream packages remain separately MIT-licensed
DeepSeek components; this package does not vendor their runtime or preset files.

The native Git Bash transport uses the installed public
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-subprocess-local`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-win32-process` and
`node-pty` interfaces. The helper and its bounded control protocol are plugin
code, not modifications to the host's private terminal implementation. The separately
installed native libraries and their license notices are not bundled here.

The persistent tool in src/tools/persistent.ts is adapted from the MIT-licensed
DeepSeek dsh-tool-bash-persistent component, Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek. The
supported Desktop 0.2.0-rc.2 and CLI 0.2.1-alpha.1 both ship the same 16041-byte
implementation (SHA-256 2cc6627cc2e02ab65960e124f8c249045024fffe2563ab3507f7fbed9872acdc).
This adaptation additionally recognizes actual incremental completion frames
and bounds its fallback buffer. It does not modify the installed host files.
The upstream MIT copyright and license notice is retained in LICENSE.
